---
/**
 * 영어 소개 페이지 (/en/about/). 한국어 소개(src/pages/about.astro)와 같은 내용을 영어로 쓴다.
 */
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import { localizePath } from '../../i18n/locales';
import { siteConfig } from '../../site.config';
import { liveTools } from '../../tools/registry';
---

<DocLayout title="About" description={`What ${siteConfig.name} is and how it handles your files.`}>
  <h2>What is {siteConfig.name}?</h2>
  <p>
    A collection of free tools that process files such as PDFs right inside your browser. There is
    nothing to install, no sign-up, and your files are never uploaded to a server.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we made it</h2>
  <p>
    Even simple jobs like merging two PDFs or rotating a page usually mean uploading your file to
    someone's server first. Few people are comfortable uploading contracts or copies of their ID to
    a server they know nothing about.
  </p>
  <p>
    Modern browsers are fast enough to do this work on their own. So we built tools that finish the
    job on your own device, without uploading anything.
  </p>

  <h2>How are files processed?</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Files are processed only inside your browser and are never sent to any server.</li>
    <li>
      Every program the tools use is downloaded from this site. Nothing is loaded from other
      companies' servers.
    </li>
    <li>
      The tool area, where you choose and process files, runs in an isolated space your browser
      keeps separate. Other scripts on the page cannot read your file content or file names, and
      nothing inside the tool area can be sent out.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can check this yourself in the Network tab of your browser's developer tools.
      <a href={localizePath('/safety/', 'en')}>See how</a>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tools you can use now</h2>
  <ul>
    {liveTools.map((tool) => (
      <li>
        <a href={localizePath(tool.href, 'en')}>{tool.text.en.name}</a>
        {`: ${tool.text.en.description}`}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>More tools, such as image conversion, are on the way.</p>

  <h2>Is it free?</h2>
  <p>
    Yes, every tool is free. The site is funded by ads. Ads are only placed outside the tool area,
    so they cannot see your files.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
